
   ============================================================================
   QFRONT.CFG — Configuration File Reference
   ============================================================================
   QFront v1.0.0 — pcbirc crew 2026

   This file documents every keyword recognized by qfront.cfg.
   Lines starting with # or ; are comments. Blank lines are ignored.


   ADDRESSES
   ============================================================================

   Address=zone:net/node[.point]
     Your FidoNet address. Multiple lines = multiple AKAs (up to 16).
     The first Address= line is your primary address.

     Examples:
       Address=1:234/56
       Address=1:234/56.1
       Address=2:5020/1234


   DIRECTORIES
   ============================================================================

   Outbound=path
     BSO outbound root directory. REQUIRED.
     Example: Outbound=C:\FIDO\OUTBOUND

   Inbound=path
     Inbound file directory. REQUIRED for receiving files.
     Example: Inbound=C:\FIDO\INBOUND

   TempInbound=path
     Temp inbound for non-password-protected sessions. Optional.
     Example: TempInbound=C:\FIDO\INBOUND\TEMP

   NetmailDir=path
     Netmail .MSG storage directory.
     Example: NetmailDir=C:\FIDO\NETMAIL


   LOGGING
   ============================================================================

   LogFile=path
     Log file path. Appended, not overwritten.
     Example: LogFile=C:\QFRONT\QFRONT.LOG

   Debug=0|1
     Verbose debug logging. Default: 0.


   SERIAL PORT
   ============================================================================

   ComPort=n
     COM port number (1-4). Default: 1.

   BaudRate=n
   LockedBaud=n
     DTE locked baud rate. Default: 115200.
     Either keyword works — they are synonyms.


   SESSION CONTROL
   ============================================================================

   MaxRetries=n
     Max call attempts per node per day. Default: 5.

   RetryDelay=n
     Seconds between retries to same node. Default: 300.

   HoldTime=n
     Seconds to hold a node after max retries exceeded. Default: 3600.


   EXTERNAL PROGRAMS
   ============================================================================

   Mailer=path
     External mailer for BinkP/IP sessions.
     Example: Mailer=C:\BINKD\BINKD.EXE

   Tosser=path
     External tosser called after successful sessions.
     Example: Tosser=C:\QFRONT\QSCAN.EXE /BOTH

   TicProc=path
     TIC file processor called after sessions.
     Example: TicProc=C:\HTICK\HTICK.EXE toss


   NODELIST
   ============================================================================

   NodelistDir=path
     Directory containing raw nodelists and compiled .NDX files.
     Example: NodelistDir=C:\FIDO\NODELIST

   NodelistBase=name
     Base name of the primary nodelist (max 8 chars, no extension).
     Example: NodelistBase=NODELIST


   SEMAPHORE FILES
   ============================================================================

   Semaphore=path:errorlevel
     Define a semaphore trigger file. When the file exists, QFront
     deletes it and exits with the given errorlevel.

     Multiple Semaphore= lines are allowed (up to 16).

     Examples:
       Semaphore=C:\FIDO\QFEXIT.NOW:0
       Semaphore=C:\FIDO\SCANMAIL.NOW:3
       Semaphore=C:\FIDO\COMPNL.NOW:4


   EVENT SECTIONS
   ============================================================================

   Events are defined as [Event.NAME] sections. Each section contains
   schedule and flag settings.

   Schedule:
     Description=text           Human-readable description
     Days=pattern               Daily | Weekdays | Weekends | sMTWtFS
     Start=HH:MM                Start time (24-hour)
     End=HH:MM                  End time (24-hour)
     Active=yes|no              Enable/disable event. Default: yes.
     Errorlevel=n               Exit code for exit-type events
     Batch=path                 Batch file to run

   Cost limits:
     MinCost=n                  Minimum allowable cost (-1 = ignore)
     MaxCost=n                  Maximum allowable cost (-1 = ignore)

   Auto-poll:
     AutoPoll=addr,addr,...     Comma-separated addresses to poll

   Flags (set as Flag=yes):
     SlideTime                  Slide start time if still processing
     EchoOnly                   EchoMail only
     NetOnly                    NetMail only
     ReceiveOnly                Don't dial out
     SendCMOnly                 Only dial CM nodes
     SendNonCMOnly              Only dial non-CM nodes
     NodeCritical               Node-critical event
     NoHeldAttach               Don't process held attaches
     ListedOnly                 Only dial listed nodes
     ForcePoll                  Force poll regardless of restrictions
     PollDuring                 Allow polling during event
     ScanBefore                 Run tosser before event
     CompileNodelist            Compile nodelist after event
     CompileOnReceive           Compile when new nodelist received
     Rescan                     Rescan areas after event
     EndNoMail                  End event when queue is empty
     ExitNoMail                 Exit program when queue is empty
     ExitWhenDone               Exit after processing outbound

   Example:

     [Event.ZMH]
     Description=Zone Mail Hour
     Days=Daily
     Start=01:00
     End=05:00
     SendCMOnly=yes
     ForcePoll=yes


   ECHOMAIL AREA SECTIONS
   ============================================================================

   Areas are defined as [Area.TAG] sections.

     Path=dir                   Message base directory
     Conference=n               PCBoard conference number
     Passthrough=Y|N            Pass-through (forward without storing)

   Example:

     [Area.NET_DEV]
     Path=C:\FIDO\AREAS\NET_DEV
     Conference=42
     Passthrough=N


   ROUTING RULES
   ============================================================================

   Routing rules are plain lines (not in sections):

     Route <pattern> direct
     Route <pattern> via <address>
     Route <pattern> host
     Route <pattern> hub <address>
     Route <pattern> hold
     Route <pattern> abshold
     NoPoll <address>

   Pattern format: zone:net/node  (use * as wildcard)

   Examples:
     Route 1:234/56 direct
     Route 1:234/* via 1:234/0
     Route 2:* via 2:5020/0
     Route * host
     NoPoll 1:999/1


   COMPLETE EXAMPLE
   ============================================================================

     # QFront v1.0.0 Configuration
     # Generated by QFConfig

     Address=1:234/56
     Address=1:234/56.1

     Outbound=C:\FIDO\OUTBOUND
     Inbound=C:\FIDO\INBOUND
     TempInbound=C:\FIDO\INBOUND\TEMP
     NetmailDir=C:\FIDO\NETMAIL

     NodelistDir=C:\FIDO\NODELIST
     NodelistBase=NODELIST

     Mailer=C:\BINKD\BINKD.EXE
     Tosser=C:\QFRONT\QSCAN.EXE /BOTH
     TicProc=C:\HTICK\HTICK.EXE toss

     LogFile=C:\QFRONT\QFRONT.LOG
     Debug=0

     ComPort=1
     BaudRate=115200
     MaxRetries=5
     RetryDelay=300
     HoldTime=3600

     Semaphore=C:\FIDO\SCANMAIL.NOW:3
     Semaphore=C:\FIDO\COMPNL.NOW:4

     Route 1:234/* via 1:234/0
     Route 2:* via 2:5020/0
     NoPoll 1:999/1

     [Event.ZMH]
     Description=Zone Mail Hour
     Days=Daily
     Start=01:00
     End=05:00
     SendCMOnly=yes
     ForcePoll=yes
     EndNoMail=yes

     [Event.NightPoll]
     Description=Nightly poll
     Days=MTWTF
     Start=23:00
     End=06:00
     ForcePoll=yes

     [Area.NET_DEV]
     Path=C:\FIDO\AREAS\NET_DEV
     Conference=42
     Passthrough=N

     [Area.FIDONEWS]
     Path=C:\FIDO\AREAS\FIDONEWS
     Conference=15
     Passthrough=N

   ============================================================================
   End of QFRONT-CFG.DOC
   ============================================================================
